{"id":"r1","level":1,"levelName":"Reading","n":1,"of":9,"title":"The first six letters","titleHe":"אָלֶף עַד וָו","goal":"Recognise א ב ג ד ה ו and know what each one sounds like.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Hebrew is written right to left, and its alphabet has twenty-two letters — all of them consonants. Vowels come later, as marks above and below. Start with six."},{"type":"letters","ids":["א","ב","ג","ד","ה","ו"],"items":[{"l":"א","name":"אָלֶף","en":"alef","sound":"silent (carries its vowel)","confuse":["ע"]},{"l":"ב","name":"בֵּית","en":"bet","sound":"b — v without a dagesh","confuse":["כ"]},{"l":"ג","name":"גִּימֶל","en":"gimel","sound":"g as in go","confuse":["נ"]},{"l":"ד","name":"דָּלֶת","en":"dalet","sound":"d","confuse":["ר","ך"]},{"l":"ה","name":"הֵא","en":"he","sound":"h","confuse":["ח","ת"]},{"l":"ו","name":"וָו","en":"vav","sound":"v — also the vowels o and u","confuse":["ז","ן"]}]},{"type":"tip","body":"א is not a sound of its own. It's a holder: it carries whichever vowel is written under it. ה is a real h at the start of a word, and silent at the end."},{"type":"tip","body":"ב is b with a dot inside it (בּ) and v without (ב). You'll meet the dot properly in lesson 8 — for now, expect both sounds."}],"vocab":[{"he":"אַבָּא","en":"dad","translit":"aba"},{"he":"בָּא","en":"comes","translit":"ba"},{"he":"גַּג","en":"roof","translit":"gag"},{"he":"דּוֹד","en":"uncle","translit":"dod"},{"he":"הוּא","en":"he","translit":"hu"},{"he":"וָו","en":"hook","translit":"vav"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What is this letter called?","options":["pe","tet","alef","shin"],"correct":2,"prompt":"א"},{"type":"choice","q":"What is this letter called?","options":["samekh","bet","ayin","dalet"],"correct":1,"prompt":"ב"},{"type":"choice","q":"What is this letter called?","options":["shin","gimel","alef","pe"],"correct":1,"prompt":"ג"},{"type":"choice","q":"What is this letter called?","options":["tet","tav","dalet","gimel"],"correct":2,"prompt":"ד"},{"type":"choice","q":"What is this letter called?","options":["kaf","chet","he","tsadi"],"correct":2,"prompt":"ה"},{"type":"choice","q":"What is this letter called?","options":["vav","tet","kaf","lamed"],"correct":0,"prompt":"ו"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["dad","an emigrant","concerning","runs"],"correct":0,"prompt":"אַבָּא","translit":"aba"},{"type":"choice","q":"Which letter is dalet?","options":["ת","ג","ד","ל"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["הוּא","בָּא","דּוֹד","אַבָּא"],"correct":2,"say":"דּוֹד","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “uncle”?","options":["מַאי","בַּיְשָׁן","דּוֹד","סִפּוּר"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “dad”?","options":["בֵּן","צֶבַע","סִיסְמָה","אַבָּא"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["אַבָּא","dad"],["בָּא","comes"],["גַּג","roof"],["דּוֹד","uncle"],["הוּא","he"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"Which letter is bet?","options":["ב","ס","כ","ח"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"Which letter is gimel?","options":["ה","ר","ט","ג"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"Which letter is vav?","options":["ר","ה","ג","ו"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “comes” in Hebrew","answer":"בָּא","hint":"ba"}]}